Taking an Irq's notification disarms it but leaves its line unmasked,
so the controller would go on forwarding a line nothing is armed on,
and the destroy of the Irq's pool, which takes the notification first, does the same;
the controller forwards a line exactly while an Irq is armed on it.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: controller forwards a line nothing is armed on

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -367,9 +367,6 @@ void irq_drop(struct cap *signalled)
     struct irq *irq = signalled_irq(signalled);
     irq_set_bits(irq, 0);
     /* Only the controller's lines have a mask. */
-    if (line_on_controller(irq->line)) {
-        irq_enable(irq->line, false);
-    }
     *signalled = (struct cap){ 0 };
 }
 
